    {
      "title": "DNS Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "DNS Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Names and Data",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==DNS== maps names to data (mostly IPs)",
                "A **distributed, hierarchical** database",
                "Read a name ==right to left==",
                "`www.example.com.` = root `.` → `com` → `example` → `www`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Who Asks Whom",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Stub resolver",
                    "sub": "your OS",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Recursive resolver",
                    "sub": "ISP, 8.8.8.8, 1.1.1.1: does the work",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Authoritative",
                    "sub": "holds the real answer for a zone",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tiers, Zones, Transport",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tier",
                "Knows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Root** (13 identities a–m, many anycast instances)",
                  "the TLD servers"
                ],
                [
                  "**TLD** (.com, .org)",
                  "the domain's NS"
                ],
                [
                  "**Authoritative**",
                  "the records"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==zone== = namespace slice one set of authoritative servers manages",
                "A ==delegation== (NS record) hands a subtree to another zone"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Transport",
              "items": [
                "{green:UDP/53} by default",
                "{orange:TCP/53} fallback: large responses (==TC bit==), zone transfers, DNSSEC-sized answers"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Stub asks, ==recursive== resolves, **authoritative** answers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Resolution Workflow Step by Step",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Resolution Workflow Step by Step",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cache Check, Then the Walk",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Browser cache",
                    "sub": "hit: stop",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OS cache + hosts",
                    "sub": "hit: stop",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolver cache",
                    "sub": "hit: stop",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Walk hierarchy",
                    "sub": "full miss only",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Cold lookup: www.example.com",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Resolver asks root",
                    "note": "referral: .com TLD NS",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolver asks TLD",
                    "note": "referral: example.com NS",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolver asks authoritative",
                    "note": "returns the A record",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Recursive vs Iterative",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Recursive",
                "Iterative"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Path",
                  "stub → resolver",
                  "resolver → root/TLD/auth"
                ],
                [
                  "Reply",
                  "==final answer== or error",
                  "best answer or ==referral==: 'ask them'"
                ],
                [
                  "Requests",
                  "**one**",
                  "**many**, asker follows each"
                ],
                [
                  "Load",
                  "resolver works and caches",
                  "each server stays cheap"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Glue Records",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Glue== = A/AAAA of a nameserver inside the zone it serves",
                "`ns1.example.com` serves example.com: {red:circular} without it",
                "The ==parent== supplies glue alongside the referral"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Both at once",
              "text": "A real lookup uses **both**: recursive from stub to resolver, iterative from resolver down the hierarchy."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Record Types That Matter",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Record Types That Matter",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Address and alias records",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==A== = name → IPv4",
                "==AAAA== = name → IPv6",
                "Many A/AAAA at one name = ==round-robin==",
                "==CNAME== = alias of another name",
                "A CNAME cannot share its name with any other record",
                "So no CNAME at the apex: use ALIAS/ANAME or A"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mail and zone records",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==MX== = mail server + priority; ==lower== is tried first",
                "MX target = hostname, never an IP or CNAME",
                "==NS== = the zone's ==authoritative nameservers==; the parent uses it to delegate",
                "==SOA== = zone serial + timers"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "dig example.com MX +short"
              ],
              "note": "10 is tried before 20"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "10 mail1.example.com.",
                "20 mail2.example.com."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compared",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Answers",
                "Gotcha"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "A",
                  "IPv4",
                  "many allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "AAAA",
                  "IPv6",
                  "many allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "CNAME",
                  "alias",
                  "never at apex"
                ],
                [
                  "MX",
                  "mail",
                  "lower wins"
                ],
                [
                  "NS",
                  "delegation",
                  "authoritative servers"
                ],
                [
                  "TXT",
                  "SPF, DKIM, DMARC, ownership",
                  "free-form text"
                ],
                [
                  "PTR",
                  "reverse IP → name (rDNS)",
                  "IP → name only"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Classic mistakes",
              "text": "==CNAME at the apex==, or an MX pointing at a ==CNAME or IP==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "TTL and Caching",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TTL and Caching",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What TTL Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==TTL== = seconds a resolver may cache a record",
                "Set **per record** by the authoritative server",
                "Counts down in the resolver's cache"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "TTL",
                "Range",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Low",
                  "60–300 s",
                  "fast changes, {red:more queries}"
                ],
                [
                  "High",
                  "3600–86400 s",
                  "fewer queries, {red:slow changes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Changing Records Safely",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Lower TTL",
                    "note": "one old TTL ahead",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Switch record",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Raise TTL",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "'Propagation' = old cached answers ==expiring==",
                "No push: you cannot force other resolvers to refresh"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Negative Cache and Flush",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==NXDOMAIN== is cached too, for the SOA minimum",
                "A just-created record can still look **missing**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "ipconfig /flushdns",
                "resolvectl flush-caches",
                "sudo dscacheutil -flushcache"
              ],
              "note": "Windows / systemd-resolved / macOS"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why lower TTL before a move?** Caches then expire fast.",
                "**Can you force propagation?** No, wait for expiry.",
                "**New record missing?** A cached NXDOMAIN."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
